.IX Title "REPOBUNDLE 1"
.TH REPOBUNDLE 1 "2026-09-04" "perl v5.34.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "NAME"
repobundle \- bundle a repository into a single text file
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBrepobundle\fR [\fIoptions\fR] [\fIpath\fR ...]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBrepobundle\fR collects text files from a Git repository or directory
and writes them as a single Markdown document to standard output.
.PP
Inside a Git repository, only tracked files are included.
.PP
For directories that are not Git repositories, files are discovered
recursively.
.PP
Individual files may also be supplied directly.
.PP
Binary files and files larger than 10 \s-1MB\s0 are skipped.
.PP
The resulting bundle is intended for inspection, sharing, archiving,
or providing complete small-project context to another tool.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.IX Header "OPTIONS"
\&\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
.PP
Show information about files as they are processed.
.PP
Diagnostic output is written to standard error so that standard output
remains suitable for redirection.
.PP
\&\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.PP
Show usage information.
.PP
\&\fB\-\-version\fR
.PP
Show the version of \fBrepobundle\fR.
.SH "PATHS"
.IX Header "PATHS"
If no path is supplied, the current directory is used.
.PP
A Git repository is bundled using its tracked files.
.PP
A non-Git directory is searched recursively.
.PP
Individual files may also be supplied.
.PP
Multiple paths may be supplied.
.PP
For example:
.PP
.Vb 3
\&    repobundle ~/Documents/project\-a
\&    repobundle ~/Documents/project\-a ~/Documents/project\-b
\&    repobundle README.md src/main.c
.Ve
.SH "OUTPUT"
.IX Header "OUTPUT"
The bundle is written to standard output.
.PP
For example:
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    repobundle > repo.md
\&
\&    repobundle | pbcopy
\&
\&    repobundle | less
.Ve
.PP
Each file is emitted as a fenced Markdown code block with a language
selected from its filename.
.PP
A header containing the repository name, generation time, file count,
and total byte count is included at the beginning of the bundle.
.SH "FILES"
.IX Header "FILES"
Inside a Git repository, files are obtained from git \fBls\-files\fR\|(1).
.PP
Binary files are skipped.
.PP
Files larger than 10 \s-1MB\s0 are skipped.
.PP
Generated bundle files ending in \fI.bundle\fR or \fI.rbundle\fR are skipped.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.IX Header "EXAMPLES"
Bundle the current repository:
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    repobundle
.Ve
.PP
Bundle a repository elsewhere:
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    repobundle ~/Documents/my\-project
.Ve
.PP
Bundle a directory recursively:
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    repobundle ~/Documents/some\-directory
.Ve
.PP
Bundle specific files:
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    repobundle README.md src/main.c
.Ve
.PP
Save the bundle:
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    repobundle > repo.md
.Ve
.PP
Copy the bundle to the macOS clipboard:
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    repobundle | pbcopy
.Ve
.PP
Inspect the generated bundle:
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    repobundle | less
.Ve
.PP
Show processing information while writing the bundle:
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    repobundle \-\-verbose > repo.md
.Ve
.SH "NOTES"
.IX Header "NOTES"
The standard output of \fBrepobundle\fR contains only the generated
bundle. Diagnostic messages from \fB\-\-verbose\fR are written to standard
error.
.PP
This allows the output to be safely redirected or piped to another
command.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBgit\fR\|(1), \fBless\fR\|(1)
